<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bhuchar Mori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1591</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bhuchar Mori was fought in 1591 near Dhrol in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Saurashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, between a Mughal army under Mirza Aziz Koka and the Kathiawar chiefs led by the Jam of Nawanagar, who had sheltered the fugitive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Muzaffar Shah III of Gujarat. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> won after heavy losses on both sides. Nawanagar then submitted to Mughal authority, and the battle is remembered as one of the largest fought in Saurashtra.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bhuchar-mori.jpg" alt="Battle of Bhuchar Mori" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mavdanji Bhimji Ratnu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sketch_of_Battle_of_Bhuchar_Mori_from_Yaduvanshprakash.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
